$DIR/main.p:43:10: cannot pass HF(c.get) to call, which keeps it after returning
    HF(c.get) points into a method value whose receiver is in MethodValue's
    frame. A method value (at main.p:43) is a record in MethodValue's frame that
    holds its receiver, and calling it calls the method on that receiver. call
    passes s to s.String (which may call main.(HF).String) (main.p:23), which
    stores h in package variable keepF (main.p:14), so HF(c.get) would outlive
    MethodValue's frame.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Change call to take a value or an owner, which it can keep: an owned[T] from
    new, a shared[T], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)

